WEBVTT

00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:07.480
<i>Tokyo Station.</i>

00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:10.440
<i>Agenda 11</i>
<b>Business Trip</b>

00:00:08.450 --> 00:00:11.240
<i>The platform for the Tokaido shinkansen.</i>

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:17.150
<i>The 7:10 AM Nozomi 9 for Hakata 
will be departing shortly.</i>

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:22.710
<i>It's been years since I joined Teiai, 
and these have been rare occasions.</i>

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:25.850
<i>Business trips to Fukuoka!</i>

00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:29.590
<i>Not only that, but the "business" will 
just consist of popping in for a meeting.</i>

00:00:30.070 --> 00:00:33.470
<i>That'll likely only take two or three hours.</i>

00:00:33.470 --> 00:00:36.840
<i>Since I'm staying overnight, 
the rest of my time can be spent...</i>

00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:38.180
<b>Sightseeing</b>

00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:41.110
<i>Sightseeing and hitting the pubs of Hakata!</i>

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:39.430
<b>Sightseeing and hitting</b>

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:41.100
<b>Sightseeing and hitting the pubs of Hakata</b>

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:45.350
<i>A bonus I never expected!</i>

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:50.940
Excuse me, Tonegawa-sensei...

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:53.110
Why are we taking the shinkansen?

00:00:53.810 --> 00:00:59.180
Well, it'd be faster to get 
to Fukuoka by plane, I think.

00:01:00.530 --> 00:01:02.120
What fun would that be?

00:01:03.030 --> 00:01:05.870
Since we've got a vaca—

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:05.870
<b>Vacation</b>

00:01:06.310 --> 00:01:09.520
Rather, a business trip where 
we have time to spare.

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:11.880
We should enjoy the trip, don't you think?

00:01:12.390 --> 00:01:13.980
It'd be a waste not to!

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:18.340
<i>Tonegawa-sensei is drinking beer?!</i>

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:24.350
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:01:18.950 --> 00:01:20.440
<i>It's true, if he drinks now,</i>

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:23.230
<i>it'll probably be out of his 
system in time for the meeting...</i>

00:01:23.230 --> 00:01:24.350
<i>But...</i>

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:28.100
Refreshments are available for purchase.

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:33.610
Would anyone care for coffee, 
tea, sandwiches, or a meal?

00:01:33.990 --> 00:01:35.690
Yeah, let me get something.

00:01:35.690 --> 00:01:36.180
Yes, sir?

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:37.560
A chi-kama.

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:40.580
<i>There's no doubt about it!</i>

00:01:40.580 --> 00:01:42.870
<i>Tonegawa-sensei is viewing 
this business trip...</i>

00:01:42.870 --> 00:01:45.670
<i>with the mindset of being 
on a little vacation!</i>

00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:46.370
with the mindset of being 
on a little vacation...

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:48.710
Thank you for your purchase.

00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:49.350
<i>That's why he almost said</i>

00:01:49.350 --> 00:01:53.750
<i>"vacation" and not "business trip" before!</i>

00:01:50.690 --> 00:01:53.750
<b>Vacation</b>

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:56.910
<i>Even if this trip isn't a big deal for work,</i>

00:01:56.910 --> 00:02:00.640
<i>should he treat it like this? 
Is this really okay?</i>

00:02:02.440 --> 00:02:07.440
That really hits the spot! 
My first beer in twenty days!

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:09.090
Twenty days?

00:02:09.090 --> 00:02:11.050
Huh? Oh...

00:02:11.050 --> 00:02:14.620
The president is always 
calling me up for something,

00:02:14.620 --> 00:02:18.900
so I practically never get any days off.

00:02:20.980 --> 00:02:25.620
Although I suppose working twenty 
days in a row isn't that rare.

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:28.120
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:02:28.660 --> 00:02:30.880
<b>What kind of idiot am I?!</b>

00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:30.880
<i>What kind of idiot am I?!</i>

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:35.130
<i>Who cares if he's treating 
this like a vacation?!</i>

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:39.760
<i>Who could blame him for enjoying a beer?!</i>

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:41.640
<i>I just have to step up!</i>

00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:42.510
<b>I will!</b>

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:44.260
<i>I will... make sure Tonegawa-sensei...</i>

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:46.130
<i>can enjoy himself!</i>

00:02:46.130 --> 00:02:48.570
<i>I will back him up!</i>

00:02:53.140 --> 00:02:53.980
Hello?

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:57.740
Where are you right now, Tonegawa?

00:02:58.580 --> 00:02:59.490
President?!

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:08.090
<i>Uh, I'm on my way to Fukuoka for 
some business at the moment.</i>

00:03:08.090 --> 00:03:11.970
I see. Maybe I called at a bad time, then.

00:03:11.970 --> 00:03:14.250
<i>Of course not, sir. Can I help you?</i>

00:03:15.830 --> 00:03:18.860
<i>Well, Tonegawa, the thing is...</i>

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:20.010
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:03:20.360 --> 00:03:22.970
What do you think of yoga?

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:25.370
Yoga... as in... yoga, sir?

00:03:25.370 --> 00:03:26.560
Yes.

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:29.650
To be honest, my lower back 
has been acting up lately.

00:03:29.650 --> 00:03:32.070
I've been looking into it,

00:03:32.070 --> 00:03:34.890
and it seems yoga is supposed 
to help quite a bit.

00:03:34.890 --> 00:03:36.020
<i>I see...</i>

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:40.640
But some of those poses seem a 
bit excessive for the elderly,

00:03:40.030 --> 00:03:41.530
<b>Tei</b>

00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:44.910
and I'm worried I may 
hurt my back even more.

00:03:45.750 --> 00:03:48.290
<i>What do you think, Tonegawa?</i>

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:51.660
Do you think I should try yoga?

00:03:56.920 --> 00:03:57.960
President...

00:03:57.960 --> 00:04:05.840
<b>The Big Book of Yoga
Let's Yoga
Yoga For Anyone</b>

00:03:58.290 --> 00:04:00.620
<i>To be totally honest, sir,</i>

00:04:00.620 --> 00:04:04.510
<i>I can't say whether or 
not you should try yoga.</i>

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:08.090
<i>I can't, but there is one thing I can say...</i>

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:11.100
<b>There is one thing I can say...</b>

00:04:08.090 --> 00:04:12.590
<i>Tonegawa feels it! This is the 
time to demonstrate his loyalty!</i>

00:04:13.190 --> 00:04:17.110
If your back pain were ever to get 
so bad that you couldn't walk,

00:04:19.160 --> 00:04:21.610
it wouldn't be a problem at all.

00:04:23.140 --> 00:04:24.510
And that's because...

00:04:24.510 --> 00:04:28.110
I would act as your walking stick!

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:35.620
President Hyoudou

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:35.620
Call Ended

00:04:33.680 --> 00:04:35.620
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:04:36.450 --> 00:04:38.880
<i>He hung up?! Wait, no...</i>

00:04:41.590 --> 00:04:43.440
<i>The call was disconnected!</i>

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:45.630
<b>The signal</b>

00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:45.630
<i>The tunnel cut the signal!</i>

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:50.390
<i>And at the worst possible time!</i>

00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:52.520
<b>Even if you couldn't walk, it wouldn't be a problem at all.
And that's because I would act as your walking stick.</b>

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:54.090
<i>Instead of this, it's only...</i>

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:55.270
<b>Even if you couldn't walk, it wouldn't be a problem at all.
And that's because</b>

00:04:53.770 --> 00:04:55.270
<b>Huh?!</b>

00:04:57.670 --> 00:05:00.160
I need to call him back! Right now!

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:01.560
As soon as I can!

00:05:01.560 --> 00:05:02.400
H-Hello?

00:05:04.890 --> 00:05:06.720
Tonegawa!

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:10.160
What did you mean by that, you bastard?

00:05:11.050 --> 00:05:14.290
<i>And you have the nerve to 
hang up on a call from me?!</i>

00:05:14.290 --> 00:05:17.470
Th-That's not it, sir! That was just—

00:05:19.510 --> 00:05:20.470
<i>Again?!</i>

00:05:21.190 --> 00:05:23.300
<b>Irritation!!</b>

00:05:21.190 --> 00:05:25.880
<i>In his irritation, Tonegawa 
desperately, diligently redials!</i>

00:05:23.320 --> 00:05:25.880
<b>Irritation!! Desperation!!</b>

00:05:24.110 --> 00:05:24.920
<b>Diligent!!</b>

00:05:24.940 --> 00:05:25.880
<b>Diligent!! Redial!!</b>

00:05:26.250 --> 00:05:27.130
<i>And yet!</i>

00:05:28.550 --> 00:05:29.360
Hello?!

00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:33.560
<i>The customer you are calling is unavailable.</i>

00:05:33.830 --> 00:05:34.560
<b>No good!!</b>

00:05:34.180 --> 00:05:37.060
<i>It's no good! Impossible!</i>

00:05:37.060 --> 00:05:39.940
<i>The president decided to block his number!</i>

00:05:38.420 --> 00:05:39.940
<b>Blocked number!</b>

00:05:43.800 --> 00:05:47.340
Unbelievable, Nozomi!

00:05:47.340 --> 00:05:50.160
Why do you have so many damn tunnels?!

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:52.740
Nozomi!

00:05:53.300 --> 00:05:57.250
<i>In the end, Tonegawa ends up 
making a U-turn in Nagoya.</i>

00:05:55.180 --> 00:05:57.250
<b>Nagoya</b>

00:05:58.810 --> 00:06:00.380
<i>Tonegawa-sensei...</i>

00:06:00.380 --> 00:06:04.150
<i>I'll follow wherever you lead, sir!</i>

00:06:04.150 --> 00:06:08.380
<i>Yamazaki cries manly tears! Tears of sorrow!</i>

00:06:08.490 --> 00:06:13.390
<b>Currently the Tokaido shinkansen has signal even when passing through tunnels.
To any salarymen watching, please relax and enjoy your vaca— business trips.</b>

00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:12.510
Would anyone like a beer or some snacks?

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:17.470
<i>Tonegawa manages to clear up the 
misunderstanding with the president,</i>

00:06:17.470 --> 00:06:18.390
<i>and attends the meeting...</i>

00:06:18.840 --> 00:06:21.380
It's gotten pretty late, hasn't it, sir?

00:06:21.380 --> 00:06:25.230
I'm in no mood for drinks anymore.

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:29.910
Hello?

00:06:30.500 --> 00:06:31.910
What?!

00:06:32.970 --> 00:06:34.070
Understood.

00:06:35.090 --> 00:06:35.910
What is it, sir?

00:06:36.570 --> 00:06:38.750
I need to do a sudden office evaluation.

00:06:38.750 --> 00:06:42.150
I'm heading straight to the Kansai office.

00:06:46.510 --> 00:06:53.060
<b>Middle Management Blues</b>

00:06:46.510 --> 00:06:53.060
<b><i>Mr. Tonegawa</i></b>

00:08:13.860 --> 00:08:18.810
<i>Yamazaki is sent back to Tokyo, 
while Tonegawa treks to the Kansai office.</i>

00:08:19.530 --> 00:08:22.180
<i>A sudden assignment that'll have 
me away from home for a week...</i>

00:08:22.830 --> 00:08:26.940
<i>And in Osaka of all places! A town 
that caters to those who love to eat!</i>

00:08:27.570 --> 00:08:31.190
<i>I never saw this coming! Now it's all 
the gourmet dining I could ask for!</i>

00:08:31.530 --> 00:08:33.030
<i>That said,</i>

00:08:33.030 --> 00:08:37.610
<i>I honestly don't know too much about 
the best places to dine in Osaka.</i>

00:08:37.610 --> 00:08:43.210
<i>But I can always just have the men in 
black who work here show me around.</i>

00:08:43.810 --> 00:08:44.580
So...

00:08:45.080 --> 00:08:49.330
Since the Kansai office's numbers 
are having trouble growing,

00:08:49.330 --> 00:08:51.760
I've been sent by the main 
office to observe things here.

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:52.590
The name's Tonegawa.

00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:57.190
I've already taken a look 
at this office's schedule,

00:08:57.190 --> 00:09:00.890
and to be frank, it's far too inefficient!

00:08:59.890 --> 00:09:01.600
<b>Inefficient</b>

00:09:02.090 --> 00:09:07.600
To get better numbers, you'll need to 
implement better time management!

00:09:08.340 --> 00:09:11.780
For the coming week, I'm going to 
be evaluating and instructing you

00:09:11.780 --> 00:09:12.990
with that in mind!

00:09:13.130 --> 00:09:15.360
<b>Psst... Psst.... Psst...</b>

00:09:15.360 --> 00:09:19.910
Now, given my position, I will 
have to be strict in that regard,

00:09:19.910 --> 00:09:22.790
but that's only when we're on the clock.

00:09:22.790 --> 00:09:24.870
When it's time to relax, I'll relax.

00:09:24.870 --> 00:09:25.710
What I'm saying is...

00:09:27.270 --> 00:09:31.460
I do enjoy the occasional drink after work.

00:09:32.970 --> 00:09:36.470
<i>He creates an atmosphere flowing 
in a positive direction!</i>

00:09:33.820 --> 00:09:36.070
<b>Positivity</b>

00:09:36.470 --> 00:09:39.690
<i>I've managed to create a good atmosphere.</i>

00:09:39.690 --> 00:09:43.310
<i>Now they'll have an easy 
time inviting me to—</i>

00:09:42.220 --> 00:09:43.310
Hey, dumbasses!

00:09:42.220 --> 00:09:43.310
<b>Dumbasses!</b>

00:09:43.850 --> 00:09:47.810
Tonegawa-sensei acts just a little nice,
and you're all ready to party?!

00:09:47.810 --> 00:09:50.190
Well, quit getting things mixed up!

00:09:50.630 --> 00:09:53.470
You're not the ones who get to relax!

00:09:53.470 --> 00:09:55.570
Just Tonegawa-sensei!

00:09:56.250 --> 00:10:00.320
<i>And just as easily, a stagnant, 
resentful atmosphere is created!</i>

00:09:56.670 --> 00:09:58.800
<b>Stagnation</b>

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:02.570
Er, that's not actually what I—

00:10:02.570 --> 00:10:06.140
Tonegawa-sensei, I'm truly sorry for 
the scene these dumbasses caused!

00:10:06.140 --> 00:10:07.480
No, I was trying to—

00:10:07.480 --> 00:10:11.770
If they've done anything to 
upset you, don't hold back!

00:10:11.770 --> 00:10:14.160
You can really let them have it!

00:10:14.160 --> 00:10:17.960
Depending on how bad it is, I, Kinezaki, 
as head of the Kansai branch,

00:10:17.960 --> 00:10:19.900
am willing to handle things personally...

00:10:19.900 --> 00:10:20.960
No, no, no!

00:10:20.340 --> 00:10:23.350
<b>Atmosphere</b>

00:10:20.960 --> 00:10:24.850
<i>This idiot! After I went to the trouble of 
creating a relaxed atmosphere, he ruined it!</i>

00:10:23.350 --> 00:10:24.850
<b>Ruined!</b>

00:10:25.300 --> 00:10:29.100
<i>This Kinezaki has turned the 
situation as sour as imaginable!</i>

00:10:30.730 --> 00:10:35.110
<i>Well, with an entire week, I suppose 
things will mellow out in time.</i>

00:10:35.590 --> 00:10:38.610
<i>And so, seven days later, 
the last day of his trip....</i>

00:10:36.210 --> 00:10:38.610
Teiai Finance

00:10:36.210 --> 00:10:38.610
<b>Day 7:
The Final Day</b>

00:10:42.530 --> 00:10:47.340
<i>The tense atmosphere has lasted all 
seven days, without a single break!</i>

00:10:51.250 --> 00:10:53.110
I'm sorry! I'm so sorry!

00:10:53.110 --> 00:10:55.310
Please forgive me!

00:10:55.720 --> 00:10:59.460
<i>Not just that, but the men in 
black are clearly terrified!</i>

00:10:59.460 --> 00:11:02.800
<i>This state of absolute tension 
is reaching its breaking point!</i>

00:11:00.570 --> 00:11:02.800
<b>Near the breaking point!!</b>

00:11:05.890 --> 00:11:07.960
<i>The last day...</i>

00:11:08.470 --> 00:11:11.370
<i>Ultimately, no one has asked 
Tonegawa out for drinks,</i>

00:11:11.370 --> 00:11:13.620
<i>and the time is currently after 5:00 PM.</i>

00:11:13.620 --> 00:11:17.070
<i>His week of overseeing this office 
has successfully concluded.</i>

00:11:17.070 --> 00:11:21.130
<i>And the air surrounding these 
men in black seems to ask,</i>

00:11:21.130 --> 00:11:23.980
<i>"Should we really let it end like this,</i>

00:11:23.980 --> 00:11:26.790
<i>without mingling with Tonegawa at all?"</i>

00:11:24.470 --> 00:11:28.080
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:11:28.900 --> 00:11:31.270
Hey! Today's the last day!

00:11:31.270 --> 00:11:33.880
Yeah... Should we really 
let it end like this?

00:11:33.880 --> 00:11:34.830
I dunno!

00:11:34.830 --> 00:11:37.650
Idiot! You do anything 
stupid and you're dead!

00:11:37.650 --> 00:11:40.840
Yeah, but on the first day,
he said he liked to go out for drinks!

00:11:40.840 --> 00:11:44.300
That was just a load of small talk!

00:11:44.710 --> 00:11:46.850
Yeah, but just look at him!

00:11:46.850 --> 00:11:50.940
Work's been over for a while 
now, but Tonegawa-sensei...

00:11:50.940 --> 00:11:53.630
He's doing a crossword puzzle!

00:11:53.630 --> 00:11:56.730
<i>Tonegawa tries to encourage 
the course of events.</i>

00:11:57.540 --> 00:11:59.740
You think he's waiting for us to ask him out?

00:12:00.230 --> 00:12:03.410
Come to think of it, 
Tonegawa-sensei wasn't that scary.

00:12:03.410 --> 00:12:05.380
Hell, he was actually kinda nice!

00:12:05.380 --> 00:12:06.810
Yeah, you're right!

00:12:06.810 --> 00:12:10.000
He's not gonna bite our heads off for 
asking him to a going-away party!

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:11.610
Now that you mention it...

00:12:11.610 --> 00:12:12.370
True.

00:12:12.370 --> 00:12:14.500
<i>Yes! It's flowing in the right direction.</i>

00:12:14.930 --> 00:12:17.540
<i>Now, press harder! Invite me...</i>

00:12:17.540 --> 00:12:19.000
<i>to a going-away party!</i>

00:12:19.730 --> 00:12:23.340
<i>Take the bait on the end of my line!</i>

00:12:24.370 --> 00:12:28.270
But is there enough time? Will he be 
able to catch his shinkansen home?

00:12:29.260 --> 00:12:33.210
Ah, hello? Yes, that's right.

00:12:33.210 --> 00:12:35.860
I'm taking the last shinkansen back.

00:12:35.860 --> 00:12:39.140
So I'll be killing time here until it leaves.

00:12:39.140 --> 00:12:40.900
Right, I appreciate it.

00:12:41.430 --> 00:12:43.480
<i>Tonegawa presses the issue!</i>

00:12:42.170 --> 00:12:46.910
<b>Pressing the issue!</b>

00:12:43.480 --> 00:12:46.910
<i>He wants to go drinking, no matter what! 
He's acting like a man starved!</i>

00:12:44.800 --> 00:12:46.910
<b>Starvation!!</b>

00:12:47.560 --> 00:12:48.880
Hey, did you hear that?!

00:12:48.880 --> 00:12:51.840
Yeah! Let's ask Tonegawa-sensei out!

00:12:51.840 --> 00:12:53.290
<i>Yes! They took the bait!</i>

00:12:54.660 --> 00:12:56.170
<i>They've bitten!</i>

00:12:56.170 --> 00:12:56.920
<i>The whole school!</i>

00:12:57.630 --> 00:12:59.670
<i>I'm getting the drinking party 
I've been waiting for!</i>

00:13:00.150 --> 00:13:04.170
<i>The flow is headed toward a 
drinking party, and it's high tide!</i>

00:13:02.320 --> 00:13:04.170
<b>High tide!!</b>

00:13:04.950 --> 00:13:06.180
Excuse me...

00:13:06.790 --> 00:13:08.680
Tonegawa-sensei, would you—

00:13:08.680 --> 00:13:10.170
Hey, dumbass!

00:13:10.680 --> 00:13:14.270
Work time is over! 
What're you still doing at the office?!

00:13:14.270 --> 00:13:15.720
Get the hell outta here!

00:13:15.720 --> 00:13:17.690
Tonegawa-sensei told us

00:13:17.690 --> 00:13:20.640
we need to be more efficient about time!

00:13:20.640 --> 00:13:23.690
Y-Yes, sir! We'll head home now!

00:13:24.170 --> 00:13:26.150
Buncha knuckleheads...

00:13:26.150 --> 00:13:29.830
I'm real sorry about the trouble these 
dumbasses caused you until the very end.

00:13:32.530 --> 00:13:34.830
Have a safe trip home, sir.

00:13:35.880 --> 00:13:36.830
<i>This guy!</i>

00:13:37.270 --> 00:13:41.460
<i>He jumped into my fishing hole!</i>

00:13:42.020 --> 00:13:43.840
<i>In the end...</i>

00:13:45.720 --> 00:13:50.350
<i>Tonegawa returns to Tokyo with a 
total drinking party count of zero.</i>

00:13:47.150 --> 00:13:50.350
Would anyone like a beer or some snacks?

00:13:51.800 --> 00:13:54.350
<i>Tonegawa-sensei... Tonegawa-sensei... 
Tonegawa-sensei...</i>

00:13:51.990 --> 00:13:54.350
Looming...

00:13:54.350 --> 00:13:57.610
<i>Damn you, Kinezaki!</i>

00:13:59.780 --> 00:14:03.110
<i>We turn back the clock to the days during 
Tonegawa's business trip to Osaka.</i>

00:14:03.430 --> 00:14:05.860
<i>In Teiai Meeting Room 3.</i>

00:14:06.250 --> 00:14:09.130
Yamazaki-san, can you check these documents?

00:14:09.130 --> 00:14:12.020
Yeah, okay. Leave them there.

00:14:12.020 --> 00:14:12.830
Sure.

00:14:13.700 --> 00:14:17.870
Saemon, you seem different than usual...

00:14:17.870 --> 00:14:21.130
Wh-What's with the pointy shoes?!

00:14:21.570 --> 00:14:23.750
Oh, you noticed?

00:14:24.280 --> 00:14:26.170
They're pointed toe shoes.

00:14:26.170 --> 00:14:28.200
I bought them in Harajuku yesterday.

00:14:28.200 --> 00:14:29.510
Now, just hold on a sec!

00:14:29.510 --> 00:14:34.390
That's no good! A man in black 
can't wear such flashy shoes!

00:14:34.980 --> 00:14:35.890
What's up?

00:14:35.890 --> 00:14:38.270
It's just... Saemon's shoes...

00:14:39.370 --> 00:14:41.770
I mean, that can't be okay, can it?

00:14:41.770 --> 00:14:43.770
Saemon! You...

00:14:44.230 --> 00:14:45.780
These shoes!

00:14:46.120 --> 00:14:48.490
Wh-Where'd you get them?

00:14:49.400 --> 00:14:50.410
Doushita-san?

00:14:50.410 --> 00:14:52.910
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:14:52.910 --> 00:14:55.330
<i>Pointed toe!</i>

00:14:55.330 --> 00:14:57.750
<i>With Saemon's flight of fancy as the trigger,</i>

00:15:01.240 --> 00:15:07.170
<i>Team Tonegawa is struck 
by a sudden fashion boom!</i>

00:15:05.150 --> 00:15:07.170
Team Tonegawa's

00:15:05.150 --> 00:15:07.170
<b>Sudden</b>

00:15:05.150 --> 00:15:07.170
<b>Fashion Boom!!</b>

00:15:07.650 --> 00:15:10.230
<i>Excluding only Yamazaki and Gonda.</i>

00:15:10.230 --> 00:15:11.660
Saemon!

00:15:11.660 --> 00:15:15.230
What's Tonegawa-sensei going to say 
when he sees you after he gets back?!

00:15:15.670 --> 00:15:19.430
It's fine. You worry too much, Yamazaki-san.

00:15:19.890 --> 00:15:23.310
Tonegawa-sensei wouldn't get mad 
over a little thing like this.

00:15:23.310 --> 00:15:27.070
As long as we get our work done, 
it shouldn't be a problem.

00:15:27.070 --> 00:15:29.190
But disruptions in order are 
signs of disrupted minds...

00:15:31.540 --> 00:15:33.680
Oh, sorry, I just...

00:15:33.680 --> 00:15:38.060
You sounded a bit like a school principal.

00:15:40.100 --> 00:15:43.210
<i>Yamazaki and Gonda are left 
without a leg to stand on!</i>

00:15:44.200 --> 00:15:45.210
I see.

00:15:45.640 --> 00:15:47.460
That does sound like a bit of a problem.

00:15:47.460 --> 00:15:49.840
I'm just trying to be 
serious when I warn them.

00:15:49.840 --> 00:15:52.930
Well, as talented as Saemon is,

00:15:52.930 --> 00:15:57.230
his comments tend to come off as more 
snide than he probably intends.

00:15:58.180 --> 00:16:00.350
Try to understand he doesn't 
mean anything by it.

00:16:00.350 --> 00:16:02.630
Then what should I do?

00:16:03.370 --> 00:16:07.350
<i>What else is there to do? Just tell them 
to stop because it's against regulations.</i>

00:16:07.350 --> 00:16:09.120
Regulations, sir?

00:16:09.120 --> 00:16:10.780
<i>What, you didn't know?</i>

00:16:10.780 --> 00:16:14.780
Teiai has a strict code of 
conduct for men in black.

00:16:14.780 --> 00:16:18.680
So just use that as your main argument.

00:16:18.680 --> 00:16:20.040
<i>I-I see.</i>

00:16:20.310 --> 00:16:23.470
You don't need to worry, because I'll 
be back at the beginning of the—

00:16:26.740 --> 00:16:28.800
Did he go into a tunnel?

00:16:29.210 --> 00:16:31.050
<i>And so, the new week begins.</i>

00:16:31.660 --> 00:16:33.300
Saemon! What the—

00:16:33.770 --> 00:16:36.300
Huh? What's the matter, Yamazaki-san?

00:16:36.300 --> 00:16:38.790
I could ask you that, stupid!

00:16:38.790 --> 00:16:41.310
You look like you're 
straight out of Rats & Star!

00:16:41.310 --> 00:16:44.050
Did you go to a tanning salon 
over the weekend?!

00:16:44.050 --> 00:16:45.860
Now, now, Yamazaki-san...

00:16:45.860 --> 00:16:47.410
You, too, Nakata!

00:16:47.410 --> 00:16:50.570
Why would you suddenly choose 
that Beckham style hair?!

00:16:51.070 --> 00:16:53.660
It's actually called a fauxhawk...

00:16:53.660 --> 00:16:54.700
It doesn't matter what it's called!

00:16:55.270 --> 00:16:58.450
It's not just you, either! 
Everyone is out of line!

00:16:58.830 --> 00:17:01.680
Don't you agree, Gonda-san?!

00:17:01.680 --> 00:17:02.830
Go—

00:17:02.180 --> 00:17:02.830
<b>Psst...</b>

00:17:05.430 --> 00:17:06.420
<i>Sparkle...</i>

00:17:07.310 --> 00:17:08.440
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:17:08.730 --> 00:17:10.800
Gonda-san, your sunglasses...

00:17:11.910 --> 00:17:14.420
The teardrop lenses look wonderful on you.

00:17:15.170 --> 00:17:18.700
I took him to Harajuku over the weekend, 
and he was crazy about them.

00:17:19.830 --> 00:17:22.390
<i>The disruption in Team 
Tonegawa's uniformity</i>

00:17:22.390 --> 00:17:24.860
<i>has reached its apex!</i>

00:17:23.240 --> 00:17:25.690
<b>Apex</b>

00:17:26.090 --> 00:17:27.530
You should join us next time, Yamazaki-san.

00:17:27.530 --> 00:17:28.450
I can't!

00:17:28.450 --> 00:17:30.320
Why are you being so—

00:17:30.320 --> 00:17:32.070
Because it's against regulations!

00:17:35.010 --> 00:17:39.180
You might be talented, 
but what's wrong is wrong!

00:17:39.180 --> 00:17:41.950
The regulations in the men in black 
guidelines have to be adhered to!

00:17:43.940 --> 00:17:45.080
What's so funny?!

00:17:45.080 --> 00:17:49.820
Well... Yamazaki-san, 
have you actually read them?

00:17:50.290 --> 00:17:52.210
Because it should say this:

00:17:52.630 --> 00:17:55.530
"Suits, neckties, sunglasses, 
and leather shoes.

00:17:55.530 --> 00:17:58.590
And they are all to be uniformly black."

00:17:59.410 --> 00:18:01.100
What are you getting at—

00:18:02.440 --> 00:18:04.350
Did you figure it out?

00:18:05.090 --> 00:18:06.600
You little snake...

00:18:07.570 --> 00:18:10.730
That's right! We're not breaking them at all!

00:18:10.730 --> 00:18:13.240
Not a single regulation!

00:18:12.130 --> 00:18:13.630
Black Sunglasses (Teardrop lenses)

00:18:12.380 --> 00:18:13.630
Black Leather Shoes (Pointed toes)

00:18:12.630 --> 00:18:13.630
Black (Bow) Neckties

00:18:12.880 --> 00:18:13.630
Black Suits (Pinstriped)

00:18:13.890 --> 00:18:17.190
<i>Black sunglasses! A black necktie, in a bow!</i>

00:18:17.190 --> 00:18:18.630
<i>A black suit!</i>

00:18:18.630 --> 00:18:20.660
<i>And black leather shoes!</i>

00:18:20.510 --> 00:18:22.640
<b>No infringements!</b>

00:18:20.660 --> 00:18:26.850
<i>Not a single infringement! In other words, 
the men in black code of conduct...</i>

00:18:22.640 --> 00:18:26.370
<b>No infringements!
Men in Black Code of Conduct</b>

00:18:26.850 --> 00:18:28.370
<i>has essentially been upheld!</i>

00:18:28.760 --> 00:18:31.450
There shouldn't be any problem at all!

00:18:35.320 --> 00:18:37.630
I see, I see.

00:18:38.050 --> 00:18:39.880
You've got a point there.

00:18:40.210 --> 00:18:43.140
Even if it sounds like a 
middle schooler making excuses,

00:18:43.140 --> 00:18:46.390
you have indeed stuck to the rules.

00:18:48.390 --> 00:18:51.980
T-Tonegawa-sensei!

00:18:53.290 --> 00:18:56.730
That said, Saemon, 
that outfit of yours is still...

00:18:56.730 --> 00:18:58.410
Out!

00:18:58.410 --> 00:19:00.280
But sir, it's not breaking any regulations!

00:19:00.790 --> 00:19:01.780
That's not the point!

00:19:02.190 --> 00:19:05.490
I'm not talking about regulations here.

00:19:05.490 --> 00:19:10.420
I'm saying that little getup of 
yours just looks ridiculous!

00:19:10.420 --> 00:19:12.920
<b>Not Fashionable</b>

00:19:10.420 --> 00:19:12.920
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:19:12.920 --> 00:19:14.680
You don't get it!

00:19:14.680 --> 00:19:17.670
None of you understand the 
fundamentals of wearing a suit.

00:19:17.670 --> 00:19:19.800
How an adult is supposed to dress!

00:19:20.220 --> 00:19:22.760
For instance, this shirt!

00:19:23.430 --> 00:19:24.470
It's loose and floppy!

00:19:28.980 --> 00:19:30.980
Your jackets, your slacks...

00:19:30.980 --> 00:19:33.850
The most basic of fundamentals 
is to take these to a tailor

00:19:33.850 --> 00:19:35.370
so they'll fit you perfectly.

00:19:35.370 --> 00:19:39.490
You can hastily slap on all the quirky 
accessories you want, but without that,

00:19:39.490 --> 00:19:42.240
it's just cosplay! 
You're embarrassing yourselves!

00:19:42.240 --> 00:19:46.810
The important thing about wearing a suit 
is making sure it's the right size,

00:19:46.810 --> 00:19:48.490
and then not going overboard.

00:19:49.220 --> 00:19:51.780
But that'd be the same as usual!

00:19:51.780 --> 00:19:53.370
How are we supposed to be fashionable?

00:19:53.370 --> 00:19:54.380
Yamazaki.

00:19:54.380 --> 00:19:56.040
S-Sir.

00:19:58.250 --> 00:19:59.710
<b>Smooth</b>

00:20:02.850 --> 00:20:04.890
T-Tonegawa-sensei...

00:20:04.890 --> 00:20:07.140
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:20:07.140 --> 00:20:11.640
He just put a handkerchief 
in his pocket... and yet...

00:20:11.640 --> 00:20:13.960
<i>Psst, psst...</i>

00:20:15.130 --> 00:20:17.060
Fashion is about subtlety.

00:20:17.060 --> 00:20:21.500
By doing that, you manage to actually 
make something look natural!

00:20:22.280 --> 00:20:24.410
A-Amazing!

00:20:23.800 --> 00:20:25.410
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:20:25.770 --> 00:20:27.200
Then these clothes...

00:20:27.690 --> 00:20:30.120
They were the ones wearing me!

00:20:30.120 --> 00:20:33.640
Saemon, where did you 
get those shoes, anyway?

00:20:33.640 --> 00:20:35.630
H-Harajuku, sir...

00:20:36.500 --> 00:20:38.880
That town never changes, it seems.

00:20:38.880 --> 00:20:44.130
T-Tonegawa-sensei, where do you 
shop for your clothes and the like?

00:20:44.510 --> 00:20:46.590
Well...

00:20:46.590 --> 00:20:50.270
Since we've got plenty of time today,

00:20:50.770 --> 00:20:54.020
why don't we all head 
to Ginza and Marunouchi?

00:20:54.020 --> 00:20:56.040
<b>Whoa!</b>

00:20:56.520 --> 00:20:59.770
<i>Style in moderation. 
The sign of refined maturity.</i>

00:21:00.870 --> 00:21:06.460
<i>This is the story of a lone man who struggles 
between his employer, the president,</i>

00:21:06.460 --> 00:21:09.790
<i>his own employees, the men in black,</i>

00:21:09.790 --> 00:21:13.910
<i>and sometimes, regional branch employees.</i>

00:21:14.980 --> 00:21:19.390
<i>Tonegawa Yukio: Middle Manager.</i>

00:22:54.730 --> 00:22:56.910
<i>Next time: "Fake."</i>

00:22:55.870 --> 00:23:00.250
<b>Fake</b>
